        {
          "block_type": "line",
          "top": 162,
          "text": "Overall: 8/10 contracts matched recalculation within tolerance; 2/10 exceeded the 20% threshold."
        },
        {
          "block_type": "line",
          "top": 180,
          "text": "Exception: Contract C-2077 showed a 56.9% variance on Services with no documented Finance Manager sign-off,"
        },
        {
          "block_type": "line",
          "top": 195,
          "text": "representing a control breach under Section 7."
        },
        {
          "block_type": "line",
          "top": 225,
          "text": "7. Prior Period Recommendations"
        },
        {
          "block_type": "line",
          "top": 249,
          "text": "- Transition from unweighted Standalone List Price to a weighted allocation approach"
        },
        {
          "block_type": "line",
          "top": 267,
          "text": "- Lower the sign-off variance threshold from 20% to a more conservative level"
        },
        {
          "block_type": "line",
          "top": 282,
          "text": "- Implement system-enforced sign-off workflow"
        },
        {
          "block_type": "line",
          "top": 315,
          "text": "8. Forward-Looking Note for Next Cycle"
        },
        {
          "block_type": "line",
          "top": 339,
          "text": "Group Finance was expected to publish an updated SSP allocation methodology introducing a Weighted Factor per"
        },
        {
          "block_type": "line",
          "top": 354,
          "text": "deliverable category later in 2025. The next cycle should re-baseline the recalculation approach using the new"
        },
        {
          "block_type": "line",
          "top": 366,
          "text": "Relative SSP formula and re-test the approval variance threshold."
        },
        {
